---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HailDashboardMap from '../../components/HailDashboardMap.astro';
import {env} from 'cloudflare:workers';
import {readWeather,feedState,dashboardMode,NWS,SPC,GREELEY,LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES} from '../../lib/weather';
import {site} from '../../data/site';
const data=await readWeather(env.DB);
const nwsState=feedState(data?.nws,data?.nwsSuccess,15);
const spcState=feedState(data?.spc,data?.spcSuccess,25);
const fmt=(s:string)=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{dateStyle:'medium',timeStyle:'short',timeZone:'America/Denver'}).format(new Date(s))+' MT';
const date=(s:string)=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{dateStyle:'medium',timeZone:'America/Denver'}).format(new Date(s));
const time=(s:string)=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{timeStyle:'short',timeZone:'America/Denver'}).format(new Date(s))+' MT';
const stateLabel=(state:string)=>state==='current'?'Current':state==='stale'?'Cached · out of date':state==='cached-error'?'Cached · latest refresh failed':'Unavailable';
const severe=data?.localAlerts.filter(a=>/severe thunderstorm|tornado|special weather statement/i.test(a.event))??[];
const broader=data?.alerts.filter(a=>!a.local)??[];
const currentReports=data?.localReports??[];
const recentReports=data?.recentReports??[];
const dashboardState=dashboardMode(currentReports.length,data?.localAlerts.length??0,recentReports.length);
const dashboardStatus={hail:{label:'Hail Reported Nearby',summary:`${currentReports.length} preliminary SPC ${currentReports.length===1?'report':'reports'} within ${LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES} miles.`},warning:{label:'Active Warning',summary:`${data?.localAlerts.length??0} active NWS ${data?.localAlerts.length===1?'alert intersects':'alerts intersect'} the regional view.`},recent:{label:'Recent Hail Event',summary:`Official hail was reported within ${LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES} miles during the past 72 hours.`},quiet:{label:'Quiet',summary:'No active local warning or nearby preliminary hail report is currently stored.'}}[dashboardState];
const successfulUpdates=[data?.nwsSuccess?.completed_at,data?.spcSuccess?.completed_at].filter(Boolean) as string[];
const datasetModified=successfulUpdates.toSorted().at(-1)??'2026-09-08';
const pageSchema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Dataset','@id':`${site.url}/hail-tracker/#dataset`,name:'Live Northern Colorado Hail Tracker Near Greeley',description:'Official active National Weather Service alerts and preliminary Storm Prediction Center hail reports prioritized within 50 statute miles of Greeley.',url:`${site.url}/hail-tracker/`,mainEntityOfPage:{'@id':`${site.url}/hail-tracker/#webpage`},dateModified:datasetModified,spatialCoverage:{'@type':'Place',name:'Approximately 50 statute miles from the Greeley, Colorado city reference point'},creator:[{'@type':'Organization',name:'National Weather Service',url:'https://www.weather.gov/'},{'@type':'Organization',name:'NOAA Storm Prediction Center',url:'https://www.spc.noaa.gov/'}],publisher:{'@id':`${site.url}/#business`},isBasedOn:[NWS,SPC]};
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control','public, max-age=60, s-maxage=300, stale-if-error=900');
---
<Layout title="Northern Colorado Hail Tracker Near Greeley" description="Official NWS alerts and preliminary SPC hail reports prioritized within 50 miles of Greeley, with distances, timestamps, freshness, and source limitations." pageSchema={pageSchema}>
  <header class={`page-head tracker-head hail-workspace dashboard-hero dashboard-hero--${dashboardState}`}><div class="dashboard-hero__content"><div class="eyebrow">Northern Colorado Hail Dashboard · Official-source context</div><div class="dashboard-status"><span class="dashboard-status__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Current status</span><strong>{dashboardStatus.label}</strong></div><h1>Know what the storm is doing—and what to check next.</h1><p>{dashboardStatus.summary} Radar, warning geometry, and preliminary hail observations are presented together without claiming damage to any specific vehicle.</p><div class="dashboard-hero__links"><a class="button" href="#live-map-heading">View Live Map ↓</a><a href="https://www.weather.gov/" class="text-link">Official NWS warnings ↗</a></div><div class="tracker-scope"><span>Geographic calculation anchor</span><strong>{GREELEY.latitude.toFixed(5)}, {GREELEY.longitude.toFixed(7)}</strong><small>City reference point only—not a business, shop, or owner address.</small></div></div></header>

  <HailDashboardMap alerts={data?.localAlerts??[]} reports={currentReports} />

  <section class="section tracker-summary dashboard-strip" aria-label="Live dashboard summary">
    <div><span>Alerts</span><strong class:list={{'status-current':nwsState==='current','status-stale':nwsState!=='current'}}>{data?.localAlerts.length??0} local</strong><small>NWS feed: {stateLabel(nwsState)}</small></div>
    <div><span>Hail reports</span><strong class:list={{'status-current':spcState==='current','status-stale':spcState!=='current'}}>{currentReports.length} nearby</strong><small>SPC feed: {stateLabel(spcState)}</small></div>
    <div><span>Radar</span><strong>NOAA/NWS MRMS</strong><small>Current reflectivity · no animation</small></div>
    <div><span>Updated</span><strong>{successfulUpdates.length?fmt(successfulUpdates.toSorted().at(-1)!):'Unavailable'}</strong><small>Feed timestamps remain detailed below.</small></div>
  </section>

  <div class="tracker-content">
    <section class="section tracker-section" aria-labelledby="local-alerts-heading">
      <div class="tracker-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">National Weather Service</div><h2 id="local-alerts-heading">Northern Colorado Active Alerts</h2></div><p>Official warning geometry is checked against the {LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES}-mile Greeley radius. When an alert has no polygon, its official area description is used as a clearly identified fallback.</p></div>
      {nwsState!=='current'&&<div class="callout tracker-warning"><strong>{stateLabel(nwsState)}.</strong> Current official alert data may be unavailable. Any retained alerts below are cached and show their expiration time. Check <a href="https://www.weather.gov/">weather.gov</a> for current warnings; this tracker never indicates an all-clear.</div>}
      {data?.localAlerts.length?<div class="alert-grid">{data.localAlerts.map(a=><article class="card alert-card"><span class="source-chip">NWS · {a.location_basis}</span><h3>{a.headline}</h3><p>{a.area}</p>{a.distance_miles!==null&&<p><strong>Nearest polygon distance from Greeley:</strong> {a.distance_miles.toFixed(1)} miles</p>}<p><strong>Expires:</strong> {fmt(a.expires_at)}</p><a href={a.source_url}>Official NWS source →</a></article>)}</div>:nwsState==='current'?<p class="empty-state">No active NWS alerts intersecting or identified with the primary Northern Colorado area were returned at the last successful refresh. Conditions can change quickly.</p>:<p class="empty-state">No cached local alert records are available.</p>}
      <details class="broader-alerts"><summary>View Broader Colorado Alerts <span>({broader.length})</span></summary><p>These active statewide alerts fall outside the primary Northern Colorado view based on official geometry or area description. They are secondary so distant Colorado events do not dominate this tracker.</p>{broader.length?<div class="alert-grid">{broader.map(a=><article class="card alert-card"><span class="source-chip">NWS · broader Colorado</span><h3>{a.headline}</h3><p>{a.area}</p><p><strong>Expires:</strong> {fmt(a.expires_at)}</p><a href={a.source_url}>Official NWS source →</a></article>)}</div>:<p>No broader Colorado alerts are currently stored.</p>}</details>
    </section>

    <section class="section tracker-section tracker-hail" aria-labelledby="hail-reports-heading">
      <div class="tracker-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">NOAA Storm Prediction Center · Preliminary</div><h2 id="hail-reports-heading">Recent Hail Reports Near Greeley</h2></div><p>Reports are sorted by occurrence time and filtered by calculated great-circle distance from the Greeley city reference point—not county name alone.</p></div>
      {spcState!=='current'&&<div class="callout tracker-warning"><strong>{stateLabel(spcState)}.</strong> Recent official hail data may be unavailable or out of date. Cached reports remain labeled with occurrence and refresh times. Missing reports do not mean no hail occurred.</div>}
      {data?.localReports.length?<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Official preliminary hail reports within {LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES} statute miles of Greeley; times shown in Mountain Time.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Reported location</th><th scope="col">Hail size</th><th scope="col">Distance</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.localReports.map(r=><tr><td>{date(r.occurred_at)}</td><td>{time(r.occurred_at)}</td><td><strong>{r.location}</strong><br/><span>{r.county} County, Colorado</span>{r.comments&&<details class="report-comments"><summary>Official report details</summary><p>{r.comments}</p></details>}</td><td>{r.size_inches.toFixed(2)} in.</td><td>{r.distance_miles.toFixed(1)} mi.</td><td><a href={r.source_url}>SPC preliminary report</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>:spcState==='current'?<p class="empty-state">No preliminary SPC hail reports within {LOCAL_RADIUS_MILES} miles of Greeley were returned for the current SPC report day. This is not proof that no hail occurred.</p>:<p class="empty-state">No cached local hail reports are available.</p>}
      <div class="damage-caveat"><strong>A nearby hail report confirms that hail was reported in the area.</strong><p>It does not confirm that a specific vehicle was damaged. A vehicle inspection is required to determine actual damage.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tracker-section" aria-labelledby="severe-heading"><div class="tracker-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Weather Awareness</div><h2 id="severe-heading">Recent Severe Weather</h2></div><p>Active local severe-thunderstorm, tornado, and relevant special-weather statements are summarized here when supplied by NWS. Follow official instructions during dangerous weather.</p></div>{severe.length?<ul class="severe-list">{severe.map(a=><li><strong>{a.event}</strong><span>{a.headline}</span><small>Expires {fmt(a.expires_at)} · National Weather Service</small></li>)}</ul>:<p class="empty-state">No active local severe-weather items in these categories are stored. This is not an all-clear; consult the National Weather Service for current conditions.</p>}</section>

    <section class="section tracker-section tracker-topo" aria-labelledby="details-heading"><div class="tracker-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Reading the Data</div><h2 id="details-heading">Hail Report Details</h2></div></div><div class="tracker-explain"><article><h3>Location and distance</h3><p>SPC supplies a reported location and coordinates. Distance is calculated from the Greeley city coordinate using the great-circle formula and rounded for display.</p></article><article><h3>Size and timing</h3><p>SPC magnitude is converted from hundredths of an inch to inches. Reports follow the SPC report day, which runs from noon UTC through 11:59 UTC the next day.</p></article><article><h3>Preliminary status</h3><p>Current SPC reports are preliminary observations with varying coverage and precision. They may be corrected and are not a complete survey of every place that received hail.</p></article></div></section>

    <section class="section tracker-section hail-size-guide" aria-labelledby="hail-size-heading">
      <div class="tracker-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">From Reported Size to Vehicle Context</div><h2 id="hail-size-heading">What reported hail sizes can mean.</h2></div><p>Familiar comparisons make official magnitudes easier to picture. They do not predict whether a particular vehicle was damaged.</p></div>
      <div class="hail-size-scale" role="list">
        <article role="listitem"><div class="hail-size-orb" style="--hail-scale:.58"><span>¾″</span></div><div><span class="hail-size-name">Penny-size</span><h3>About ¾ inch</h3><p>Small hail may leave no obvious marks or may create shallow dents that are difficult to see outdoors.</p></div></article>
        <article role="listitem"><div class="hail-size-orb" style="--hail-scale:.72"><span>1″</span></div><div><span class="hail-size-name">Quarter-size</span><h3>About 1 inch</h3><p>Visible dents become more plausible, especially on broad horizontal panels exposed to wind-driven hail.</p></div></article>
        <article role="listitem"><div class="hail-size-orb" style="--hail-scale:.88"><span>1¼–1½″</span></div><div><span class="hail-size-name">Half dollar to ping-pong ball</span><h3>1.25–1.50 inches</h3><p>Multiple panels can show distributed dents, but severity still depends on the storm and vehicle.</p></div></article>
        <article role="listitem"><div class="hail-size-orb" style="--hail-scale:1.04"><span>1¾–2″</span></div><div><span class="hail-size-name">Golf ball to hen egg</span><h3>1.75–2.00 inches</h3><p>Deeper impacts, sharper dents, trim damage, and glass risk become more likely.</p></div></article>
        <article role="listitem"><div class="hail-size-orb" style="--hail-scale:1.18"><span>2″+</span></div><div><span class="hail-size-name">Hen egg and larger</span><h3>More than 2 inches</h3><p>Significant panel deformation and damage beyond PDR suitability are possible. Follow warnings and remain sheltered.</p></div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="hail-damage-evidence"><figure><picture><source media="(max-width: 720px)" srcset="/images/auto-hail-damage-before-after-peak-country-greeley-co-720.webp"/><img src="/images/auto-hail-damage-before-after-peak-country-greeley-co.webp" width="1088" height="1446" alt="Before and after comparison of distributed hail dents repaired on a dark vehicle roof at Peak Country" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture><figcaption>An authentic Peak Country repair example showing distributed roof damage before repair and the completed result.</figcaption></figure><div><div class="eyebrow">Damage is vehicle-specific</div><h3>Reported size is context—not a diagnosis.</h3><p>Damage varies with wind speed, impact angle, storm duration, hail density and hardness, whether the vehicle was moving or sheltered, and the material, shape, bracing, finish, and orientation of each panel.</p><p>Even relatively shallow dents can disappear in ordinary daylight. Controlled PDR reflection lighting helps reveal changes in panel shape that photographs and outdoor inspection can miss.</p><a href="/hail-size-guide/">Read the complete hail-size guide →</a></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tracker-section tracker-history" aria-labelledby="history-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Separate from the Live Feed</div><h2 id="history-heading">Five-Year Hail History</h2><p>Verified NOAA/NCEI Storm Events observations are presented in the current 2022–2026 five-calendar-year window. The 2026 live season remains preliminary and separate from completed historical records.</p></div><a href="/northern-colorado-hail-history/">Explore Northern Colorado Historical Hail →</a></section>

    <section class="section tracker-section sources-panel" aria-labelledby="sources-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Source Transparency</div><h2 id="sources-heading">Official Data Sources</h2></div><div><p><strong>Active alerts:</strong> <a href={NWS}>National Weather Service API</a></p><p><strong>Preliminary hail reports:</strong> <a href={SPC}>NOAA Storm Prediction Center</a></p><p><strong>Server cache:</strong> Cloudflare D1 retains the last successfully ingested official records. Refresh status and timestamps above identify stale or failed-source states.</p><a href="/data-sources/">Read methodology and limitations →</a></div></section>

    <nav class="section tracker-links" aria-label="Related hail and repair resources"><a href="/hail-size-guide/">Understand Hail Size →</a><a href="/after-a-hailstorm/">What to Do After a Hailstorm →</a><a href="/auto-hail-repair/">Auto Hail Repair →</a><a href="/paintless-dent-repair/">Paintless Dent Repair →</a><a href="/service-area/">Mobile Service Area →</a><a href="/about/">About Peak Country →</a><a href="/free-hail-inspection/">Free Initial Assessment →</a></nav>
    <section class="section home-final-cta dashboard-inspection-cta"><div><div class="eyebrow">Vehicle-specific answers</div><h2>Not sure whether your vehicle was affected?</h2><p>Hail damage can be difficult to see without clean panels, controlled reflection lighting, and a direct inspection. Start with a free, no-obligation conversation.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/get-started/">Get Started</a><a href="/free-hail-inspection/">Free Initial Assessment →</a><a href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>Call {site.phoneDisplay}</a></div></section>
    <div class="hail-mountain-transition" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
